{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Init.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Init.Omega"],"declarations":54,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.route_a_verdict","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.route_a_verdict","kind":"theorem","line":371,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L371-L381","doc":"**Route-A verdict, assembled.** The slope reading dies on `5₂`; the\nconnection-count reading survives both knots; and C1 is not the quantum\nA-polynomial. (That the surviving scalar reading still cannot *equal* the\nchirality-split datum is\n`FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.symmetric_scalar_blind_to_chirality` — which is why the\nprogramme pivots to Route C.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.r1_connection_reading_survives","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.r1_connection_reading_survives","kind":"theorem","line":365,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L365-L369","doc":"**R1 (connection-count / `L`-degree reading) SURVIVES the cross-knot gate.**\nBoth knots' connection counts lie in the DT spectrum (`4₁ ↦ 3`, `5₂ ↦ 4`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.r2_slope_reading_refuted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.r2_slope_reading_refuted","kind":"theorem","line":358,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L358-L363","doc":"**R2 (slope reading) is REFUTED on the cross-knot gate.** The reading holds at\n`4₁` (`|slope| = 4 ∈ {3,4}`) but fails at `5₂` (`|slope| = 10 ∉ {3,4}`), so\n\"DT integer = boundary slope\" is a single-knot coincidence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a41Connections","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a41Connections","kind":"def","line":354,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L354-L356","doc":"`4₁` number of boundary-parabolic connections `= L`-degree of the full\nA-polynomial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.fiveTwoConnections_eq_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.fiveTwoConnections_eq_four","kind":"theorem","line":351,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L351-L352","doc":"**The full derived `A_{5₂}` has `L`-degree `4`** (geometric `3` + abelian `1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.fiveTwoConnections","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.fiveTwoConnections","kind":"def","line":347,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L347-L349","doc":"`5₂` number of boundary-parabolic connections `= L`-degree of the full\nA-polynomial: abelian + the three of the geometric component. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.fiveTwoMaxAbsSlope_derived","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.fiveTwoMaxAbsSlope_derived","kind":"theorem","line":340,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L340-L345","doc":"**`10` is the maximal absolute slope of the derived polygon**: every edge has\n`|slope| ≤ 10` (as `|dM| ≤ 10·|dL|`) and some edge attains it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.fiveTwoMaxAbsSlope","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.fiveTwoMaxAbsSlope","kind":"def","line":336,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L336-L338","doc":"`5₂` maximal absolute boundary slope. Derived: `a52_edge_slopes_in_0_m4_m10`\n+ `a52_slopes_attained` (slope `−10` is attained, nothing beyond it). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.dtSpectrum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.dtSpectrum","kind":"def","line":333,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L333-L334","doc":"The certified DT spectrum (both `4₁` and `5₂`; chirality-split at `5₂`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a52_mirror_edge_slopes_in_0_4_10","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a52_mirror_edge_slopes_in_0_4_10","kind":"theorem","line":317,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L317-L324","doc":"The mirrored `5₂` edges carry slopes `{0, 4, 10}` — the literature set as\nusually printed, i.e. the derived triangulation is the mirror of *that*\nconvention's `5₂` (which of the two is Rolfsen's is a convention no held source\nsettles). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lProfile_mirror","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lProfile_mirror","kind":"theorem","line":310,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L310-L315","doc":"**The `L`-profile is mirror-invariant** — so the `L`-degree (`R1`) is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.absSlopeEq_mirror","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.absSlopeEq_mirror","kind":"theorem","line":303,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L303-L308","doc":"**The absolute boundary slope is mirror-invariant** — so the `R2` input is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.instDecidableAbsSlopeEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.instDecidableAbsSlopeEq","kind":"instance","line":300,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L300-L301","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.absSlopeEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.absSlopeEq","kind":"def","line":296,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L296-L298","doc":"Absolute slope `|s|`, as the disjunction \"slope `s` or slope `−s`\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.isVertical_mirror","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.isVertical_mirror","kind":"theorem","line":292,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L292-L294","doc":"Verticality is mirror-invariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.slopeEq_mirror","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.slopeEq_mirror","kind":"theorem","line":284,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L284-L290","doc":"The mirror negates every slope: `v` has slope `s` iff `mirrorPt v` has slope\n`−s`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.mirrorPt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.mirrorPt","kind":"def","line":281,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L281-L282","doc":"The mirror on exponents: `M ↦ M⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a52FullLDegree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a52FullLDegree","kind":"def","line":264,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L264-L265","doc":"Full `A_{5₂}` = geometric × the abelian factor `(L − 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a52_geom_L_degree_eq_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a52_geom_L_degree_eq_three","kind":"theorem","line":262,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L262-L262","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a52GeomLDegree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a52GeomLDegree","kind":"def","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L259-L260","doc":"`L`-degree of the derived geometric `A_{5₂}`: the largest `L`-exponent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lProfile","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lProfile","kind":"def","line":256,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L256-L257","doc":"The `L`-exponent profile of a monomial list. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a52_slopes_attained","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a52_slopes_attained","kind":"theorem","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L249-L254","doc":"Each of the three slopes is attained. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a52_edge_slopes_in_0_m4_m10","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a52_edge_slopes_in_0_m4_m10","kind":"theorem","line":242,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L242-L247","doc":"**Every `5₂` Newton edge has boundary slope in `{0, −4, −10}`**, and none is\nvertical — the derived boundary-slope set, in the derived frame. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a52Edges","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a52Edges","kind":"def","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L233-L240","doc":"The six edges of the `5₂` Newton polygon (counter-clockwise). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a52_hull_subset_monomials","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a52_hull_subset_monomials","kind":"theorem","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L230-L231","doc":"Every hull vertex is a monomial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a52Reflect_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a52Reflect_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L225-L228","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a52_monomials_reciprocal_symmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a52_monomials_reciprocal_symmetric","kind":"theorem","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L220-L223","doc":"**The `5₂` monomial set is centrally symmetric** — the exponent-level shadow\nof `A_involution`, and the transcription check on the list. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a52_hull_reciprocal_symmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a52_hull_reciprocal_symmetric","kind":"theorem","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L216-L218","doc":"**The `5₂` hull is centrally symmetric.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a52Reflect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a52Reflect","kind":"def","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L213-L214","doc":"The central reflection of the `5₂` Newton polygon about `(7, 3/2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a52Monomials","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a52Monomials","kind":"def","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L206-L211","doc":"All twelve monomials of the derived `A_{5₂}`, in `(M-exp, L-exp)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a52Hull","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a52Hull","kind":"def","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L201-L204","doc":"Convex-hull vertices of the `5₂` Newton polygon, counter-clockwise, in\n`(M-exp, L-exp)`. (The producer records them as `(deg_L, deg_M)`:\n`(0,14),(1,4),(2,0),(3,0),(2,10),(1,14)`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.c1_slope_ne_a41_slope","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.c1_slope_ne_a41_slope","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L178-L181","doc":"**C1 is not the quantum A-polynomial of `4₁`.** Its Newton slope `1/2` is not\nthe `4₁` boundary slope `4`: cross-multiplying, `1 * 1 ≠ 4 * 2`. Route A therefore\nrequires the genuine colored-Jones recursion `Â_K`, not the binding carrier. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.c1_edge_slopes_pm_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.c1_edge_slopes_pm_half","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L172-L176","doc":"**C1's Newton slopes are `±1/2`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.c1NonVerticalEdges","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.c1NonVerticalEdges","kind":"def","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L167-L170","doc":"The non-vertical C1 edges (the edge `(1,2) → (−1,2)` is vertical). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.c1Hull","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.c1Hull","kind":"def","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L164-L165","doc":"Convex-hull vertices of the C1 Newton polygon. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a41_full_L_degree_eq_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a41_full_L_degree_eq_three","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L154-L156","doc":"**The full `4₁` A-polynomial has `L`-degree `3`** — the number of\nboundary-parabolic `SL₂(ℂ)` connections `{0, g, ḡ}`, and the other DT integer. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a41FullLDegree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a41FullLDegree","kind":"def","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L150-L152","doc":"`L`-degree of the **full** A-polynomial: the geometric component times the\nabelian factor `(L − 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a41GeomLDegree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a41GeomLDegree","kind":"def","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L147-L148","doc":"`L`-degree of the **geometric** component (`L²` is its top power). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a41MaxAbsSlope","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a41MaxAbsSlope","kind":"def","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L143-L145","doc":"The maximal absolute boundary slope of `4₁` is `4` — a member of the certified\nDT spectrum `{3,4}`, which is what motivated the slope reading `R2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a41_edge_slopes_pm_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a41_edge_slopes_pm_four","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L137-L141","doc":"**Every `4₁` Newton edge has boundary slope `±4`.** No edge is vertical, and\neach is slope-equal to `+4` or `−4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a41Edges","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a41Edges","kind":"def","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L130-L135","doc":"The four edges of the `4₁` Newton polygon. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a41Reflect_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a41Reflect_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L123-L128","doc":"The reflection is an involution (so the symmetry above is a genuine\npairing). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a41_monomials_reciprocal_symmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a41_monomials_reciprocal_symmetric","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L117-L121","doc":"**The full monomial set is centrally symmetric too** — the reciprocal\nsymmetry `(M,L) ↦ (M⁻¹,L⁻¹)` of the A-polynomial, at the level of exponents.\nThis is the integrity check on the typed-in polynomial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a41_hull_reciprocal_symmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a41_hull_reciprocal_symmetric","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L112-L115","doc":"**The `4₁` Newton polygon is centrally symmetric** (hull level): the\nreflection permutes the hull vertices. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a41Reflect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a41Reflect","kind":"def","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L109-L110","doc":"The central reflection of the `4₁` Newton polygon about its centre `(4,1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a41Monomials","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a41Monomials","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L93-L96","doc":"All monomials of `A_{4₁}` (geometric component), including the three\nedge-interior points `(2,1), (4,1), (6,1)` that are not hull vertices. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a41Hull","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.a41Hull","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L90-L91","doc":"Convex-hull vertices of the `4₁` Newton polygon, counter-clockwise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.intSlope","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.intSlope","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L80-L81","doc":"The integer slope `s` as an edge vector `(s, 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.instDecidableSlopeEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.instDecidableSlopeEq","kind":"instance","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L77-L78","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.slopeEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.slopeEq","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L73-L75","doc":"Slope equality by cross-multiplication: `dM₁/dL₁ = dM₂/dL₂`. Avoids rationals\nso the whole file stays in core `Int`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.instDecidableIsVertical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.instDecidableIsVertical","kind":"instance","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L70-L71","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.isVertical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.isVertical","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L66-L68","doc":"An edge is **vertical** (parallel to the `M`-axis, i.e. `dL = 0`); such edges\ncarry no boundary slope. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.edgeVec","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.edgeVec","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L63-L64","doc":"The edge vector `(dM, dL)` between two lattice points. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.Pt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteANewtonPolygonDT.Pt","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteANewtonPolygonDT.lean#L60-L61","doc":"A Newton-polygon lattice point `(M-exponent, L-exponent)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}